{
  "name": "How to Choose the Right Ramp for Your Doorway",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Picking the perfect ramp can seem tricky, but it's all about matching it to your specific needs! First off, you'll want to measure the 'rise' – that's the vertical height from the ground to the top of your threshold. This measurement is key because it determines the ramp's length to get that ideal 1:12 slope for easy use. Don't forget to check the width of your doorway and consider how the door swings. You don't want a ramp that blocks it! Next, think about the environment: will it be exposed to the elements? That helps decide between durable rubber or lightweight aluminum. You'll also need to consider if you need a fixed ramp, perhaps for a permanent solution, or something adjustable for more temporary situations. Lastly, confirm the ramp's weight capacity to ensure it can safely support whoever, or whatever, will be using it. If your threshold is irregular, or you need to ensure accessibility compliance, a professional can really help guide you through these choices and even handle custom installations.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
